## VERDICT
## **ACCEPT** setenv / unsetenv SECRET-sink parity with env_set
SPRINT **6.1** names `env_set` in SECRETSINK (landed with 2.3). Peer 2
probed the four-way SECRET surface live on the shipping host:

`env_set`  vs  `setenv`  vs  `unsetenv`  vs  `env_get`

**SECRET IDENT refuse is parity** across all four on `emit-c` and
`emit-llvm` (rc≠0 + `ERR\tsecret\<sink> sink refuses SECRET <name>`).

**`setenv` ≡ `unsetenv` ≡ `env_set`** on every SECRET axis measured
(value IDENT, key IDENT, string-lit no-FP, 3-arg extra, llvm dual).
Official smoke covers `env_set` + `setenv` only; this peer filled
**`unsetenv`** (not a product gap — same refuse).

**`env_get` is not product-parity** with the write-side trio. It is the
only lowered / `is_known_name` env op, so `check` actually prints
`ERR\tsecret`. `env_set` / `setenv` / `unsetenv` die first at
`ERR\ttype\tundefined variable` (`check_drive.oo` typecheck L64 before
`check_secret_println_sinks` L106). That is the same residual the
runtime auditor named (R-check / R-lower). **Not a setenv≠unsetenv
split. Not a SECRET false-negative on emit.**

Do **not** claim: product `oo_env_set` / `oo_setenv` / `oo_unsetenv`;
`check` dual-path `ERR\tsecret` for the write-side names; `is_sealed_env`
lists `setenv`/`unsetenv` (it lists `env_set` + `getenv` only);
`getenv` is a SECRETSINK (it is not — SECRET IDENT is **not** refused).

## CLAIM UNDER PRESSURE
| Slice | Path-A claim | Peer 2 gate |
|-------|--------------|-------------|
| 6.1 `env_set` in SECRETSINK | emit refuse SECRET IDENT | `ERR\tsecret\tenv_set sink refuses SECRET token` rc=1 |
| `setenv` sibling (2.3 / smoke) | same refuse | `… setenv sink refuses SECRET token` rc=1 |
| `unsetenv` sibling (source list, **no official rail**) | same refuse | `… unsetenv sink refuses SECRET token` rc=1 |
| `env_get` control (product op) | refuse SECRET **key** | `… env_get sink refuses SECRET token` rc=1 |
| String-lit spelling of SECRET name | no `ERR\tsecret` | all four: `sec=0` |
| `setenv` ≡ `unsetenv` ≡ `env_set` | write-side parity | **PASS** (emit + llvm + check-type residual) |
| `env_get` ≡ write-side | full product parity | **FAIL** (check + lower only) — residual, not 6.1 FN |

