SOURCE PARITY (write-side names)
---

| Site | env_get | env_set | setenv | unsetenv |
|------|---------|---------|--------|----------|
| `c_secret_is_sink_name` (`c_emit_secret_alias.oo:16`) | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| `c_secret_emit_guard` a1 family (L117) | yes | yes | no | no |
| `c_secret_emit_guard` a1+a2 6.1 family (L157) | no | yes | yes | yes |
| `c_secret_emit_guard` full `args` scan (L214–218) | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| `check_secret_println_sinks` (`c_emit_secret.oo:204` / `:239`) | argi=1 eq_only | argi≥1 | argi≥1 | argi≥1 |
| `is_sealed_env` | yes | yes | **no** | **no** |
| `is_known_name` / product lower | yes | **no** | **no** | **no** |

`env_set` is listed in **both** guard families (a1-only **and** a1+a2).
Harmless overlap. `setenv`/`unsetenv` rely on the 6.1 branch + full args
scan — live refuse of key **and** value IDENTs proves that is enough.

Host ELF (`nm`): `c_secret_is_sink_name` `T` @ `0x45c1c0`,
`c_secret_emit_guard` `T` @ `0x461080`, `check_secret_println_sinks`
`T` @ `0x475c50`. Refuse format is assembled
(` sink refuses SECRET ` in rodata), not a per-sink static string.

